#, no-wrap
msgid "How to minimize the amount of usage spent processing and running a job."
msgstr "Paano mabawasan ang dami ng paggamit na ginagastos sa pagpoproseso at pagpapatakbo ng isang job."

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minimize job run time"
msgstr "I-minimize ang oras ng pagpapatakbo ng job"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minimize job run time {#minimize-job-run-time}"
msgstr "I-minimize ang oras ng pagpapatakbo ng job {#minimize-job-run-time}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There are several ways you can limit the amount of time spent processing and running a job:\n"
msgstr "May ilang paraan para mabawasan ang oras na ginagastos sa pagpoproseso at pagpapatakbo ng isang job:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run only as many shots as you need: A job's QPU consumption (and therefore, its cost) scales with the number of shots. Therefore, you can manage your cost by running only as many shots as you need. For Estimator jobs, lower precision typically requires more shots and therefore a longer execution time.\n"
msgstr "Magpatakbo lang ng kasing dami ng shots na kailangan mo: Ang QPU consumption ng isang job (at samakatuwid, ang gastos nito) ay lumalaki kasabay ng bilang ng shots. Kaya naman, maaari mong pamahalaan ang iyong gastos sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo lang ng kasing dami ng shots na talagang kailangan mo. Para sa mga Estimator job, ang mas mababang precision ay karaniwang nangangailangan ng mas maraming shots at samakatuwid ay mas matagal na oras ng pagpapatakbo.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set limits on execution time:  You can limit how long each job, batch, or session runs.  For details, see the [Maximum execution time](/guides/max-execution-time) guide.\n"
msgstr "Magtakda ng limitasyon sa oras ng pagpapatakbo:  Maaari mong limitahan kung gaano katagal tumatakbo ang bawat job, batch, o session.  Para sa mga detalye, tingnan ang [Maximum execution time](/guides/max-execution-time) guide.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use only the necessary settings for error suppression and error mitigation, because higher values can cause your jobs to run longer. See [Introduction to options](/guides/runtime-options-overview), [Configure error suppression](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques), and [Configure error mitigation](error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques) for details.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin lang ang mga kinakailangang setting para sa error suppression at error mitigation, dahil ang mas mataas na mga halaga ay maaaring magpahaba ng oras ng pagpapatakbo ng iyong mga job. Tingnan ang [Introduction to options](/guides/runtime-options-overview), [Configure error suppression](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques), at [Configure error mitigation](error-mitigation-and-suppression-techniques) para sa mga detalye.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- If you are running multiple jobs that contain the same (likely parameterized) circuits and are using an error mitigation method that requires noise models, such as PEA and PEC, consider using `NoiseLearner`. With this helper program, you can learn the noise model of a circuit once and reuse the model in subsequent Estimator queries. Note that a noise model becomes stale after a certain time, so this is only practical if there is no long delay between jobs (for example, within a session). See [Noise learning helper\n"
"](/guides/noise-learning) for more details.\n"
msgstr ""
"- Kung nagpapatakbo ka ng maraming job na naglalaman ng parehong (malamang na parameterized) circuits at gumagamit ng error mitigation method na nangangailangan ng noise models, tulad ng PEA at PEC, isaalang-alang ang paggamit ng `NoiseLearner`. Sa helper program na ito, matututuhan mo ang noise model ng isang circuit nang isang beses at magagamit muli ang model sa mga susunod na Estimator query. Tandaan na ang noise model ay nagiging stale pagkalipas ng ilang panahon, kaya praktikal lang ito kung walang mahabang pagitan sa pagitan ng mga job (halimbawa, sa loob ng isang session). Tingnan ang [Noise learning helper\n"
"](/guides/noise-learning) para sa higit pang mga detalye.\n"

